From: Pocket DS Linux maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: try the next DSC when pingpong parity differs

The non-paired allocator aborts at the first available DSC whose parity
does not match the assigned pingpong. After the lower, uncompressed panel
takes pingpong 0, the returning compressed upper panel can receive
pingpong 1. A free DSC 0 then prevents consideration of the usable DSC 1.

Skip the incompatible DSC, without advancing the pingpong or reserving
the incompatible resource. Exhaustion still returns -ENAVAIL. The paired
allocator and all resource ownership checks remain unchanged.

This candidate is tested against extracted real C functions, not yet
accepted by physical lid/suspend tests.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_rm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_rm.c
@@ -539,7 +539,7 @@ static int _dpu_rm_dsc_alloc(struct dpu_rm *rm,
 
 		ret = _dpu_rm_pingpong_dsc_check(dsc_idx, pp_idx);
 		if (ret)
-			return -ENAVAIL;
+			continue;
 
 		global_state->dsc_to_crtc_id[dsc_idx] = crtc_id;
 		num_dsc++;
